; (F4d) STOP (0F 9E; README "F4 (part D)"). Measured on the socket (validation/v35s/dma.py
; f4_stop, receipts f4-f4_stop-socket{,-2}.json): the CPU goes quiet (no bus cycle) until NMI;
; the first cycle after it comes 2^19 + 38 clocks after NMI's edge (the oscillator's settling
; count), into the NMI handler with IE 1 or 0; an unmasked INTP0 edge during STOP neither
; releases it nor is remembered (its IF stays 0). STOP does not set STBC's SBF (a store sets it).
; The routine is HALT's loop with no take test (WO50): a mark word (cnt=stop, its own word: a word
; with a count field cannot jump) sets the stop state; then B tests the release (the controller's
; settling count after NMI in place of its wake) every second clock, the other word only jumps
; back. The release's E pops the instruction after STOP, whose dispatch takes NMI. This file sorts
; last (after xfer_dma.uasm): no other routine's ROM address moves.
routine stop op=9E page=0f why="(F4d) STOP: released by NMI alone, 2^19 clocks after it (f4_stop); (WO50) the wait is HALT's two-word loop without the take test; function only"
    halt cnt=stop                           ; STOP's mark (v35_intc: the stop state set; the release is the settling count's end)
st_b: halt jnc=DN:st_a                      ; B: the release test
    e                                       ; E: the instruction after STOP (its dispatch takes NMI)
st_a: halt jmp=st_b                         ; back to B (no take test in STOP)
